@startuml
title AISafe - Deployment and Replication (Physical view)

left to right direction
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11

actor "Client\n(Postman)" as Client

node "Host: localhost (or Docker network aisafe-net)" as Host {

  node "auth-service" as AuthSvc {
    node "auth-1\nhttps://localhost:8051\nprofile: instance1" as AU1
    node "auth-2\nhttps://localhost:8052\nprofile: instance2" as AU2
    database "H2 mem\nauth1" as AUD1
    database "H2 mem\nauth2" as AUD2
    AU1 --> AUD1
    AU2 --> AUD2
  }

  node "aircraft-service" as AircraftSvc {
    node "aircraft-1\nhttps://localhost:8081\npeers: 8082" as AC1
    node "aircraft-2\nhttps://localhost:8082\npeers: 8081" as AC2
    database "H2 mem\naircraft1" as ACD1
    database "H2 mem\naircraft2" as ACD2
    AC1 --> ACD1
    AC2 --> ACD2
    AC1 <--> AC2 : peer forwarding\nHTTPS
  }

  node "airport-service" as AirportSvc {
    node "airport-1\nhttps://localhost:8091\npeers: 8092" as AP1
    node "airport-2\nhttps://localhost:8092\npeers: 8091" as AP2
    database "H2 mem\nairport1" as APD1
    database "H2 mem\nairport2" as APD2
    AP1 --> APD1
    AP2 --> APD2
    AP1 <--> AP2 : peer forwarding\nHTTPS
  }

  node "route-flight-service" as RouteSvc {
    node "route-1\nhttps://localhost:8071\npeers: 8072" as RF1
    node "route-2\nhttps://localhost:8072\npeers: 8071" as RF2
    database "H2 mem\nroute1" as RFD1
    database "H2 mem\nroute2" as RFD2
    RF1 --> RFD1
    RF2 --> RFD2
    RF1 <--> RF2 : peer forwarding\nHTTPS
  }

  node "maintenance-service" as MaintSvc {
    node "maintenance-1\nhttps://localhost:8061\npeers: 8062" as MT1
    node "maintenance-2\nhttps://localhost:8062\npeers: 8061" as MT2
    database "H2 mem\nmaintenance1" as MTD1
    database "H2 mem\nmaintenance2" as MTD2
    MT1 --> MTD1
    MT2 --> MTD2
    MT1 <--> MT2 : peer forwarding\nHTTPS
  }
}

Client --> AuthSvc : HTTPS\nPOST /auth/login -> JWT
Client --> Host : HTTPS + JWT\nany replica of any service

RouteSvc --> AircraftSvc : HTTPS/REST\nJWT + X-Service-Key
RouteSvc --> AirportSvc : HTTPS/REST\nJWT + X-Service-Key
RouteSvc --> MaintSvc : HTTPS/REST\nJWT + X-Service-Key
MaintSvc --> AircraftSvc : HTTPS/REST\nJWT + X-Service-Key

legend bottom left
  10 independent Spring Boot processes: 5 services x 2 replicas, one Spring profile per replica
  (application-instance1/2.properties: server.port, datasource URL, peer list, instance id).
  Each replica owns its own in-memory H2 store; no data is shared or copied between replicas.
  Data partitioning: a record lives on the replica that created it. Generated ids are UUIDs,
  so ids never collide across replicas; natural keys (registration number, IATA code,
  model name) are checked on peers before creation (409 if they already exist).
  Calls between services: the caller holds the list of both provider replicas and fails over
  to the second one if the first does not answer (connect 1 s, read 2 s).
  TLS: server.ssl with a PKCS12 self-signed keystore (generated by scripts/gen-certs.sh,
  not committed); every replica trusts it. Secrets (JWT key, service key) come from env vars.
  auth-service replicas hold the same bootstrapped users, so they need no forwarding.
  Optional: the same topology in docker-compose, using container names as hostnames.
endlegend
@enduml
